% Manual source specification: portable Yang–Mills tracker launcher
% Output: docs/plans/yang-mills-mass-gap/bin/ym
% Existing conventional operations utility; not registered as a generated Rust unit.
% No claim of automated PDD regeneration. Preserve approved LAN intent fb139368.

Implement the existing ym list/show/say/new/close shell interface in Bash 3.2+.
The canonical Linux host owns the PDD installation and serialized tracker. A LAN
worker only needs Bash and OpenSSH; it forwards operations to the canonical host.

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Resolve the launcher's physical repository path, including symlinked
entry points and paths with spaces, using tools available on macOS and Linux.
R2 (MUST NOT): Require GNU readlink -f or GNU realpath on a Mac worker.
R3 (MUST): Read trusted machine-local .pdd/ym-lan.env for remote routing. When
YM_HOST is set, preserve every argument as literal data over batch-mode SSH,
including whitespace, quotes, dollars, semicolons and backticks. Bound connection
setup time and retain host-key verification. Clear forwarding on the canonical
invocation; the canonical config MUST leave YM_HOST unset to avoid a route loop.
R4 (MUST NOT): Run local PDD, flock or create a local tracker for remote requests;
reject remote new with exit 2 before SSH.
R4a (MUST): When the launcher runs from a git worktree of the repository, the canonical root is the MAIN checkout (the parent of git's common directory), not the worktree: every worktree on the canonical host reads and writes the same tracker. Outside git, and in the main checkout, the root is the launcher's own repository root. YM_MATHPHYSICS_ROOT still overrides.
R5 (MUST): Locally execute the existing PDD work commands in the canonical root,
export local-only/update-skip settings and preserve flock serialization of writes.
R6 (MUST): Resolve local packet filenames for new without GNU realpath.
R7 (MUST NOT): Generate keys, accept host identities, disable SSH checks, launch
models, edit peer configuration, or transmit anything except the requested
tracker operation as a side effect of this launcher.
</contract_rules>

Verification: independent shell-process fixtures for local canonical routing,
remote routing with no local PDD, trusted env routing, rejected remote creation,
literal metacharacters, relative packet names and symlinked launcher entry points.
Also require a separate live Mac/SSH/tracker receipt before calling the LAN done.
